cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MirrorLab in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "MirrorLab: real-time webcam filters, facial expressions and hand gestures on the CPU"
abstract: >-
  MirrorLab is a cross-platform computer-vision playground that turns a webcam into a
  real-time demo of facial expression recognition and hand gesture control. It reads 52
  ARKit-style blendshape channels for expressions and classifies 21 hand landmarks with
  declarative geometric rules, then stacks 54 chainable video filters and 15 procedural
  augmented-reality effects on top. It is CPU-only, runs on macOS, Windows and Linux, and
  includes a browser demo. Detection degrades gracefully across five backend rungs —
  MediaPipe Tasks, MediaPipe Solutions, OpenCV YuNet, OpenCV Haar and none — so the
  application keeps running when a model or runtime is unavailable. No frames are ever
  transmitted; the only network access is a one-time download of the model bundles.
